harness_limitations[5]: The compatibility case schema has one primary fixture only; it cannot provide a separately named pre-query file for --slurpfile or --rawfile.,"The runner now supports adapter trailing_args for --args, --jsonargs, and --; those cases use explicit witnesses because the source descriptions do not provide literal trailing values.","The runner invokes tools directly rather than through Unix, PowerShell, or cmd.exe, so shell-specific quoting examples cannot be reproduced exactly.","The schema has no terminal, platform, or timing fields, so color/NO_COLOR, --binary, and --unbuffered examples are not exact executable cases; raw version/help/build cases are informative only.","The runner now supports omit_query for --help, --version, --build-configuration, and --run-tests; -f still requires a separate filter fixture, which this task does not own."
coverage_notes[36]{id,source_line,kind,query,input,invocation,disposition,reason,evidence_case_id,expected_output}:
  invoking.input-stream-prose,16,prose-semantics,.,"1 true [2]",null,new,Representative fixture added for the documented behavior.,manual.invoking.whitespace-stream,null
  invoking.unquoted-foo,25,inline-cli-snippet,foo,null,jq foo,new,Added the exact unquoted filter invocation; it is expected to fail query compilation.,manual.invoking.unquoted-filter,null
  invoking.foo-diagnostic,26,fenced-diagnostic,foo,null,jq foo,new,The same compile-error case exercises the fenced diagnostic; exact wording is not used as the cross-tool contract because jq and tq diagnostics differ.,manual.invoking.unquoted-filter,"foo is not\ndefined"
  invoking.shell-powershell,33,inline-cli-snippet,".[\\\"foo\\\"]","{\"foo\":1}","jq '.[\\\"foo\\\"]' in PowerShell",adapted,Exercises the documented post-shell argv through the shared field-filter case. PowerShell/cmd tokenization is outside this direct-exec harness.,manual.invoking.shell-unix,null
  invoking.shell-cmd,34,inline-cli-snippet,".[\\\"foo\\\"]","{\"foo\":1}","jq \".[\\\"foo\\\"]\" in cmd.exe",adapted,Exercises the documented post-shell argv through the shared field-filter case. PowerShell/cmd tokenization is outside this direct-exec harness.,manual.invoking.shell-unix,null
  invoking.user-function-prose,36,prose-semantics,"def f: .foo; f","{\"foo\":42}",null,new,Representative fixture added for the documented behavior.,manual.invoking.user-function,null
  invoking.null-input-option,40,option-description,null,null,jq --null-input/-n FILTER,new,"The source gives option semantics but no literal FILTER; the new case uses [1,2] as a synthesized executable witness.",manual.invoking.null-input,null
  invoking.raw-input-option,44,option-description,null,null,jq --raw-input/-R FILTER,new,The source gives option semantics but no literal lines; the new case uses one/two as a synthesized executable witness.,manual.invoking.raw-input,null
  invoking.slurp-option,48,option-description,null,null,jq --slurp/-s FILTER,new,The source gives option semantics but no literal sequence; the new case uses 1/2 and length as a synthesized executable witness.,manual.invoking.slurp,null
  invoking.compact-output-option,52,option-description,null,null,jq --compact-output/-c FILTER,new,The source gives formatting semantics but no literal object; the new case uses a synthesized nested object and records raw bytes.,manual.invoking.compact-output,null
  invoking.raw-output-option,56,option-description,null,null,jq --raw-output/-r FILTER,new,The source gives string-output semantics but no literal value; the new case uses hello as a synthesized executable witness.,manual.invoking.raw-output,null
  invoking.raw-output0-option,60,option-description,null,null,jq --raw-output0 FILTER,new,The source gives NUL-framing semantics but no literal values; the new case uses a/b as a synthesized executable witness.,manual.invoking.raw-output0,null
  invoking.join-output-option,64,option-description,null,null,jq --join-output/-j FILTER,new,The source gives separator semantics but no literal values; the new case uses a/b as a synthesized executable witness.,manual.invoking.join-output,null
  invoking.sort-keys-option,72,option-description,null,null,jq --sort-keys/-S FILTER,new,The source gives key-order semantics but no literal object; the new case uses a synthesized nested object and records raw bytes.,manual.invoking.sort-keys,null
  invoking.color-option,76,option-description,null,null,jq --color-output/-C or --monochrome-output/-M FILTER,new,The source gives both options but no literal object; new cases use a synthesized object. Raw output is informative because ANSI formatting is tool/environment dependent.,null,null
  invoking.no-color,78,prose-environment-example,.,"{\"foo\":1}",NO_COLOR=1 jq FILTER,adapted,Tests forced color overriding NO_COLOR under redirected capture; terminal auto-detection requires a PTY.,manual.invoking.no-color-forced,null
  invoking.jq-colors,80,prose-environment-example,.,"{\"z\":1,\"a\":2}",JQ_COLORS=... jq -C '.',new,The source names JQ_COLORS without a concrete value; the new case uses an explicit synthesized palette and records raw bytes as informative.,manual.invoking.jq-colors,null
  invoking.tab-option,82,option-description,null,null,jq --tab FILTER,new,The source gives indentation semantics but no literal object; the new case uses a synthesized nested object and records raw bytes.,manual.invoking.tab-output,null
  invoking.indent-option,86,option-description,null,null,jq --indent n FILTER,new,The source leaves n/filter symbolic; the new case instantiates n=4 with a synthesized nested object and records raw bytes.,manual.invoking.indent-output,null
  invoking.unbuffered-option,90,option-description,null,null,jq --unbuffered FILTER,new,"The new case exercises the option with synthesized multiple inputs, but the harness can validate only final values, not flush timing.",manual.invoking.unbuffered,null
  invoking.stream-reduce-foreach-prose,98,prose-capability,reduce inputs as $event (0; . + 1),"[1,2]",null,new,Representative fixture added for the documented behavior.,manual.invoking.stream-reduce,null
  invoking.stream-errors-fence,103,fenced-stream-error-output,.,"[\"a\",n]",jq --stream-errors '.',new,The fenced output is exercised by the same exact stream-errors case; diagnostic wording remains a documented reference-vs-implementation difference.,manual.invoking.stream-errors,null
  invoking.seq-option,111,option-description,null,null,jq --seq FILTER,new,The source gives framing semantics but no literal RS/LF fixture; the new case uses a synthesized two-record JSON sequence and records raw bytes.,manual.invoking.seq,null
  invoking.from-file-option,115,option-description,.,"{\"foo\":42}",jq -f program-file,new,Representative fixture added for the documented behavior.,manual.invoking.from-file,null
  invoking.library-path-option,119,option-description,null,null,jq -L directory FILTER,new,The source gives no concrete module/directory/filter; the new case uses the repository's explicit module fixture as a synthesized executable witness rather than claiming an exact source command.,manual.invoking.library-path,null
  invoking.args-named-prose,127,prose-capability,"$ARGS.named[\"foo-bar\"]","null",null,new,Representative fixture added for the documented behavior.,manual.invoking.args-named,null
  invoking.args-option,141,option-description,null,null,"jq --args '$ARGS.positional[]' ...",new,The source gives the positional-argument contract but no concrete values; the new case uses foo/bar as an explicit executable witness via trailing_args and is not claimed as a literal source invocation.,manual.invoking.args,null
  invoking.jsonargs-option,145,option-description,null,null,"jq --jsonargs '$ARGS.positional[]' ...",new,"The source gives the positional-JSON contract but no concrete values; the new case uses 1 and {\"a\":2} as explicit executable witnesses via trailing_args and is not claimed as a literal source invocation.",manual.invoking.jsonargs,null
  invoking.exit-status-option,149,option-description,null,null,jq --exit-status/-e FILTER,new,"The source gives four status rules but no literal FILTER/input pairs; new cases instantiate false, null, empty, and true as executable witnesses.",null,null
  invoking.halt-error-prose,153,prose-capability,halt_error(7),"\"failure\"",null,new,Representative fixture added for the documented behavior.,manual.invoking.halt-error,null
  invoking.binary-option,155,option-description,.,"\"line\\nnext\"",jq --binary/-b FILTER,adapted,Tests flag acceptance and output on this host; Windows CRLF translation requires a Windows runner.,manual.invoking.binary-portable,null
  invoking.version-option,159,option-description,null,null,jq --version/-V,new,The new omit_query case executes the exact option; raw output is informative because the source gives no expected version string and tq/jq versions differ.,manual.invoking.version,null
  invoking.build-configuration-option,163,option-description,null,null,jq --build-configuration,new,The new omit_query case executes the exact option; raw output is informative because the source explicitly says its structure may change.,manual.invoking.build-configuration,null
  invoking.help-option,167,option-description,null,null,jq --help/-h,new,The new omit_query case executes the exact --help option; raw output is informative because help text is version/build dependent and the source supplies no expected text.,manual.invoking.help,null
  invoking.argument-terminator,171,option-description,null,null,jq -- ...,new,The source supplies no trailing value; the new case executes -- before the filter as an explicit option-termination witness.,manual.invoking.argument-terminator,null
  invoking.run-tests-option,175,option-description,null,jq --run-tests test-file grammar,"jq --run-tests [filename]",new,The new omit_query/stdin case executes the documented run-tests mode with a minimal concrete grammar witness; tq is deliberately marked supported so an unsupported-capability observation is exposed.,manual.invoking.run-tests,null
